    "body": "Problem:\n- `<` before a listitem (`< - foo`) is not concealed.\n- Codeblock HTML has extra blank lines.\n- Codeblock in a listitem ends the listitem, so HTML docs drop the rest\n  of the item and its nesting. Example from `:h nvim_open_win()`:\n  ```\n        • border: … the double-box style can be specified as: >\n          [ \"╔\", \"═\" ,\"╗\", \"║\", \"╝\", \"═\", \"╚\", \"║\" ].\n    <\n          If fewer than eight chars are given, they will be repeated.\n        • bufpos: …\n\n    tree-sitter-vimdoc v4.1.0:\n      (block\n        (line_li (prefix) (line) (codeblock (code (line)))))\n      (block\n        (line)                                  ; \"If fewer…\"\n        (line_li (prefix) (line) (line)))       ; \"bufpos\"\n\n    tree-sitter-vimdoc v4.2.0:\n      (block\n        (line_li (prefix) (line) (codeblock (code (line)))\n          (line))                               ; \"If fewer…\"\n        (line_li (prefix) (line) (line)))       ; \"bufpos\"\n  ```\n\nSolution:\n- Bump tree-sitter-vimdoc to v4.2.0. https://github.com/neovim/tree-sitter-vimdoc/pull/174\n- gen_help_html: get listitem indent from its first line\n- gen_help_html: don't double codeblock newlines.\n- highlight query: conceal `<` in `line_li`.\n- docs: fix doc sources where a blank line was missing after listitems\n  followed by non-listitem text.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-15T11:03:26Z",
